tion {:value "9000277"} "15 kilometres (Freestyle), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000278"} "50 kilometres (Mass Start, Classical), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000279"} "30 kilometres Skiathlon, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000280"} "4 × 10 kilometres Relay, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000281"} "Team Sprint (Freestyle), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000298"} "10 kilometres (Freestyle), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000299"} "30 kilometres (Mass Start, Classical), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000300"} "15 kilometres Skiathlon, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000301"} "4 × 5 kilometres Relay, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000302"} "Team Sprint (Freestyle), Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "2114"} "2002"] "\n" [:option {:value "2162"} "2006"] "\n" [:option {:value "923583"} "2010"] "\n" [:option {:value "350075"} "2014"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019721"} "2022"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000142"} "2026"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/193"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Sprint (Classical), Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "13 February 2018"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/937"} "Alpensia Cross-Country Centre, Alpensia Resort, Mountain Cluster, Daegwallyeong"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/9000286"} "68 from 28 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Final standings based on time achieved in last round competed in."]] [:tr {} [:th {:valign "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "Course Length: 1,176 m" [:br {}] "Height Differential: 27 m" [:br {}] "Maximum Climb: 25 m" [:br {}] "Total Climbing: 43 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The two dominant female cross-country sprinters were Norway’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/118799"} "Maiken Caspersen Falla"] " and Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/128586"} "Stina Nilsson"] ". Sochi gold medalist Falla, was also the reigning world champion and winner of the sprint ranking in the World Cup for the last three years. Nilsson was runner-up for the last two years in the World Cup, but in the current season she won three World Cup races, two in the freestyle and one in the classical style. In light snowfall, with strong winds, and in freezing cold temperatures, both skiers showed their potential throughout the competition. They clocked the fastest times in the qualifying round, won their respective quarter-final heats and finished one-two, when they competed in the same semi-final. " [:a {:href "/athletes/128475"} "Laurien van der Graaff"] " from Switzerland, twice sprint winner this season, but a specialist in the freestyle, did not qualify for the final, after finishing fifth in her semi-final."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the final, Nilsson and Falla were confronted with another Swede, " [:a {:href "/athletes/118764"} "Hanna Falk"] ", USA skier [Jessie Diggins](,  and two Olympic Athletes from Russia, " [:a {:href "/athletes/137792"} "Yuliya Belorukova"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/137794"} "Nataliya Nepryayeva"] ". Of these, only Belorukova could make any impact on the battle between the two favorites. She stayed on the heels of Nilsson when she started her attack in the second climb. Falla went past the Russian on the inside to move into second place. But Nilsson was clearly superior, and stormed to her first Olympic gold three seconds ahead of Falla. In the last descent, Belorukova closed in on Falla and both fought head-to-head on the final stretch. But Falla secured the silver 0.3 seconds ahead of Belorukova, who took home an unexpected bronze. Nepryayeva, Falk and Diggins were a considerable way behind in fourth, fifth and sixth place respectively."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/128586"} "Stina Nilsson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "3:08.74 (1)"] [:td {} "3:10.90 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "3:10.52 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "3:03.84 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/118799"} "Maiken Caspersen Falla"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NOR.png"}] "NOR"]] [:td {} "3:09.13 (2)"] [:td {} "3:11.98 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "3:10.55 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "3:06.87 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/137792"} "Yuliya Belorukova"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ROC"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ROC.png"}] "ROC"]] [:td {} "3:18.26 (15)"] [:td {} "3:14.29 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "3:10.12 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "3:07.21 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/137794"} "Nataliya Nepryayeva"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ROC"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align